cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MEE — a bilingual gamified learning application for Electrical and Electronic
  Measurements, with app-generated instrument figures"
message: "If you use this software or its instructional design in teaching or research, please cite this record."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Iulian-Teodor
    family-names: Voicila
    affiliation: "National University of Science and Technology POLITEHNICA Bucharest"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6033-2934"
  - given-names: George-Calin
    family-names: Seritan
    affiliation: "National University of Science and Technology POLITEHNICA Bucharest"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7009-2615"
  - given-names: Bogdan-Adrian
    family-names: Enache
    affiliation: "National University of Science and Technology POLITEHNICA Bucharest"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9979-3837"
repository-code: "https://github.com/BulyK47/mee-app"
abstract: >-
  A bilingual (Romanian/English) progressive web application that teaches the
  university course "Măsurări Electrice și Electronice" through short,
  gamified lessons. The design combines a Duolingo-style lesson ladder with a
  domain-specific twist: every figure is a parametric SVG instrument rendered
  from the exercise data (analog meters, oscilloscope screens, bridges,
  wattmeter connections, operational-amplifier configurations), formulas are
  typeset natively with MathML, and progress is rewarded with instruments for
  a virtual laboratory bench. It also includes spaced repetition of mistakes
  and an exam simulation mode. The question bank itself is not distributed.
keywords:
  - engineering education
  - gamification
  - electrical measurements
  - progressive web app
  - spaced repetition
  - bilingual learning
